If you are trying to sacrifice monsters on a low level of the dungeon where
larger (and therefore heavier) monsters start appearing, and you are having
trouble getting them to the altar (either carrying them there or getting
them to die on it), here is a hint that may make it easier:

You will need at least 7 boulders that you can get into the room with the 
altar.  Wait for either a dwarf with a pick-axe or a giant to help you get
some boulders.  When you have enough, use the boulders to surround the altar
like this:

	+-------------+
	|.............|
	|......'_'....|
	|......'@'....-
	-......'''....|
	|.............|
	+--------|----+

Stand where the '@' is and zap your wand of create monster.  The monster will
always appear on the altar and if you can kill it fast enough, it won't get a
chance to move off.  You can also wait on other monsters to move onto the
altar, as their only way to get to you is through the opening in the boulders
(which just happens to be where the altar is).  This strategy can be
disrupted by giants walking off with your boulders or by monsters destroying
your boulders with pick-axes or wands of striking, but otherwise works very
well.

As a samurai with the Tsurungi and speed boots, I can kill most monsters 
within a round or two and not give them a chance to move.  I even got a
dragon to die there!  With a couple of well-charged wands of create monster,
it's a great way to get your diety to love you.
